We can break down the multiplication into smaller parts:
$$2.4 \times 0.2 = (2 + 0.4) \times (0 + 0.2)$$
Using the distributive property, we can expand the expression:
$$= 2 \times 0 + 2 \times 0.2 + 0.4 \times 0 + 0.4 \times 0.2$$
Simplifying further, we get:
$$= 0 + 0.4 + 0 + 0.08$$
$$= 0.48$$
Therefore, $2.4 \times 0.2 = \boxed{0.48}$.

